sargo: Synaptics RMI4 touchscreen

The Pixel 3a touch IC is a Synaptics DSX (RMI4) at I2C 0x20 on QUPv3 SE9
(dtbo S4 PVT: synaptics_dsx@20 on qupv3_se9_i2c). SE9 is at 0xa84000, the
same GENI engine, clocks (wrap1 s1, RCG 0x18148) and SDA/SCL pins (GPIO6/7
function 1) that sweet_touch.c drives, so its I2C code is reused in the new
bsd/dev/sargo_touch.c. New pieces: reset TLMM GPIO99, IRQ GPIO125, bus
switch GPIO135 low (AP, not SSC), touch power PM660 GPIO12 output high
through the SPMI arbiter v5 write channel (only if the APID is APPS-owned
and the pin is not already on), I2C at 400 kHz, and RMI4 after Linux
drivers/input/rmi4: PDT scan, F01 configured/no-doze, F12 register
descriptors, control 8 max x/y, data1 objects. Polled every 8 ms while
touched or the IRQ line is low, else every ~100 ms; reports panel pixels
to SweetHIDTouch. SweetHIDTouch takes the panel height from boot-arg
sweettouch_panel_h (sweet 2400 by default, sargo 2220) instead of a fixed
1080x2400, so the edge-swipe zone and the mapping into the presented
1125x2436 display match the 1080x2220 panel. Boot-args: sargotouch=0,
sargotouchdelay=<s> (default 20).

